WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:09.840
The 2020 election has shown just how
profoundly education politics have

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.610
shifted. For decades, Republicans used
education to demonstrate compassion and

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.650
signal the sincerity of their commitment
to equal opportunity. Democrats used

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:24.060
education to show that they were more
interested in offering a hand up than in

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.670
handouts. Today, neither side is all that
concerned about assuaging the middle or

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.710
signaling pragmatism. Education is now
playing an amped-up role in primary

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.620
campaigns. In 2016, Donald Trump hammered
Jeb Bush with the Common Core. In 2020,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.670
Trump has energetically embraced school
vouchers and used them to draw a sharp

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.780
contrast with Democrats. In the
Democratic primary, candidates have raced

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.520
to one-up each other on free college,
loan forgiveness, and teacher pay. Whether

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.020
Trump or a Democrat claims the White
House in 2020, it's clear that the winner

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.399
will be less inclined to compromise and
more likely to stick with the more

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.740
partisan playbook. Welcome to education's new normal.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.760
Do you think education

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.040
will be a big issue in the 2020 election?
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.729
what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:23.030
sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

